 "name": "Dodrio",
 "notes": [
  "Painted design: orange-brown body (1) and three heads (12, 13, 21, two discs each; the dark dot is the eye hole in the mesh, not paint) painted as short downy strokes; black lower body (2) the same, darker; six pink tail plumes (6-11) painted as long vertical barb streaks; black crest feathers (15, 19, 27, 32, 36, 40) with long streaks; tan legs and feet (14) with a fine painted reticulate scale pattern and yellow claws; dark leathery necks (23, 30, 38) with a painted cell pattern; cream beaks (16, 20, 26, 31, 35, 41) with faint marbling; red tongues (17-28 strip) and mouth parts (29-42).",
  "So: down on the body and heads (short, soft, along the painted strokes), slightly longer on the black lower body; tail plumes and crest feathers as fine barbs along the painted streaks (long, thin, low relief); legs and necks keep their painted reticulation as the only micro relief (skin grain, no new cells); beaks smooth with a little gloss; claws, tongues and mouth untouched.",
  "Body shader 3116720224 has no normal sampler: in game only _dif and _par load; relief is faint baked cavity in _dif plus AO in _par G; Body_nor is cache-only.",
  "2026-11-14 in-game review (4K, SNAP_MODS_AB): at point-blank range the down read darker and streaky; down/lower_body cav halved, alb_amp x0.6, bake_ao 0.3 -> 0.15.",
  "Round 2 (11-14): round 1 looked too dark and streaky up close (baked AO 0.15 plus albedo strand streaks, with no normal in game). Dodrio is a bird: body down and plumes are feathers, so fur_locks with wide soft tips (down 15x8 texels, plumes 26x7) read as overlapping feather tips at mid range; albedo streaks cut to a third, baked AO to 0.04, because the twin shader now shows the real normal."
 ],
